diff --git a/09_reviews/decisions.md b/09_reviews/decisions.md
index 67b4c78..3d0e5f3 100644
--- a/09_reviews/decisions.md
+++ b/09_reviews/decisions.md
@@ -902,3 +902,26 @@ This log registers the major strategic and structural decisions made during the
 * **Alternatives rejected:** Blocking all resource inspection behind registration; reusing fictional demonstration data during adaptation; silently persisting generated copies; replacing users' saved copies when an original changes; moving workflow execution into Kosh.
 * **Open questions:** Apply and verify the Kosh migration, validate live email recovery and member persistence with controlled accounts, approve publication, and approve formal reuse terms separately. No legal reuse terms or tested-provider claims are introduced by this change.
 * **Ownership:** Website Steward leads; Narrative Editor, Proof and Governance Auditor, and Documentation Steward responsibilities guide content and handoff. Work was implemented in one task.
+
+
+### Decision 34: Strengthen Clarity Square Around a Private, Reviewed Project Journey
+* **Date:** 2026-10-12
+* **Area:** Clarity Square discovery, onboarding, account reliability, assistant actions
+* **Status:** Local implementation; publication and hosted account/provider QA pending.
+* **Decision:** Add Clarity Square to the public floating navigation and improve it in three slices: persistence/session reliability, focused onboarding, and assistant/project/task continuity. Use Home, Projects, Assistant, and More as the shared desktop/mobile hierarchy. Keep supporting tools available progressively. Show examples separately from member input and explicitly label session-only community interactions.
+* **Rationale:** A member should capture their actual problem, review a useful next move, save it as a private project, and return with context intact. Existing concepts and local prototypes must not imply shared community persistence or completed writes.
+* **Source:** KC's request to work on the platform, add the navigation entry, and implement all improvement areas phase by phase. KC separately approved restoration of the existing Platform project.
+* **Implementation:** Authenticate assistant requests and fetch owned saved context server-side; clear private client state on session changes; show confirmed saves and failures; add recovery/confirmation controls, editable memory, task provenance, concrete approval previews, restored draft state, stale-workspace rejection, and immutable approval receipts with a unique claim before execution.
+* **Affected files:** `website/src/app/clarity-square/`, `website/src/app/api/clarity-square/assistant/route.ts`, `website/src/lib/clarity-square/`, shared Navbar, Clarity Square tests, and `docs/clarity-square-improvement-plan.md`.
+* **Alternatives rejected:** Saving seeded examples as real member context; declaring writes complete before persistence; trusting browser-supplied persisted context in the assistant API; automatically replaying interrupted approvals; expanding community features before the private core is reliable.
+* **Verification boundary:** Live RLS/claim tests used transaction fixtures and rolled back all records. Controlled browser tests intercept authentication, email and model requests. Neither proves real email delivery or a complete hosted authenticated journey.
+* **Open questions:** Approve a scoped public release, then verify real confirmation/recovery links, hosted provider responses, and returning sessions on two devices. Community persistence remains a separately scoped future slice.
+* **Ownership:** Website Steward leads, with Documentation Steward and Proof and Governance Auditor responsibilities applied in this task.
+
+
+#### Decision 34 clarification — 2026-10-12
+* **[Fact] Founder priority:** KC explicitly selected “Help someone clarify an idea and move a project forward” as the primary job during the whole-platform UX review.
+* **[Fact] Approved and implemented locally:** KC approved the full simplification direction. Home and Projects are now the two main destinations; an opened project contains Conversation, Next steps and Details. Account/privacy controls share one account menu. Community stays outside the daily workflow, and loop review becomes the contextual Review progress action. This supersedes the four-destination hierarchy in the initial implementation above.
+* **Evidence:** Controlled desktop/mobile review reproduced the saved-project opening defect and identified overlapping surfaces. Full recommendations are recorded in `docs/clarity-square-improvement-plan.md` under UX simplification review.
+* **[Fact] Continuity:** Project opening now selects the actual project and updates its URL; back/reload restore the workspace. Existing projects, folders, tasks, memories, messages and plans remain supported. Archive/restore updates project status without deleting related records. Signup needs email and password; username and focus preferences are optional later.
+* **Verification boundary:** Lint, TypeScript, ten route tests and the production build pass. Controlled production-preview browser checks cover the simplified idea-to-project flow, confirmed/failed saves, restored drafts, archive/restore, account entry and responsive layouts. Hosted email/provider and two-device checks remain outstanding; the public site has not been deployed from this work.
